1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Anthropic just announced two new models: Claude Fable 5 and Claude Mythos 5. Two names — but one brain underneath.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Think of it as one engine with two different cowlings. Fable 5 goes to the public with safety classifiers built in. Mythos 5 is the full-power version, locked behind a gate for vetted researchers and cyber defenders.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Why split them at all?

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Because the underlying model is genuinely that capable. Anthropic's own researchers said releasing it unconstrained could cause serious damage. So they built safety into the product architecture itself — not as a brochure promise, but as actual code.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,000
How does it work for the person using it?

6
00:00:42,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Fable 5 runs background classifiers watching for risky requests — cybersecurity, biology, chemistry, distillation attacks. When one fires, it falls back to the older Claude Opus 4.8. And that safety net triggers on less than five percent of sessions.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Five percent. That's surprisingly low.

8
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:11,000
It means they built a model so powerful they couldn't let it run loose, but smart enough that the guardrails barely get in anyone's way.

9
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,000
And the benchmarks?

10
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Fable 5 scored eighty percent on SWE-Bench Pro versus sixty-nine for Opus 4.8. Stripe told Anthropic they compressed months of engineering into days on a fifty-million-line Ruby codebase.

11
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:29,000
But the story that matters most is in the biology labs.

12
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Mythos 5 accelerated protein drug design roughly ten times. Nine out of fourteen targets produced strong candidates. And it's the first model to consistently produce novel scientific hypotheses rather than just recombining known approaches.

13
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:55,000
A model that can suggest entirely new molecular pathways. That's not just faster — that's a different relationship between human need and scientific possibility.

14
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Exactly. And the safety holds up too. External red teams spent over a thousand hours trying to jailbreak Fable 5 and came up empty. Zero harmful outputs across thirty different attack techniques.

15
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,000
They built the walls first and the building second.

16
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Anthropic's head of product put it best: they're in a race to the top — provide technology that does asymmetrically more good than harm.

17
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Starting June twenty-third, usage credits will be required. Ten dollars per million input tokens, fifty per million output. But the customers I've heard from say the return on intelligence justifies the price.

18
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:46,000
What I'm seeing isn't just faster chatbots. It's a company that looked at its own creation, realized it was powerful, and made the hard decision to split it and build safety into the architecture.

19
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:54,000
That's the warmest version of the AI story I've heard all year. Same brain, two masks — and for now, that's more than enough.
